00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:29.080
There's no place for you in our club.

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:30.120
Itsuki!

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:32.870
Acting impolite to an upperclassman
and getting violent?

00:02:32.870 --> 00:02:34.300
You really have no right to join after all--

00:02:34.040 --> 00:02:34.910
What the hell?!

00:02:34.910 --> 00:02:36.870
Stop it, Maeshima, Kiryama!

00:02:36.870 --> 00:02:38.160
Ken!

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:40.240
What's up? Did something happen?

00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:41.240
Coach!

00:02:41.240 --> 00:02:45.490
Right now, our team has been practicing
with Himekawa as the ace.

00:02:45.490 --> 00:02:47.580
Don't forget me! I'm here, too!

00:02:47.580 --> 00:02:49.620
Be quiet for a minute.

00:02:49.620 --> 00:02:52.330
I don't want to add an outsider
at such an important time.

00:02:52.330 --> 00:02:53.240
Do you get it?

00:02:53.240 --> 00:02:55.790
This is <i>team</i> figure skating--
the skate-leading club.

00:02:55.790 --> 00:02:57.080
I know that!

00:02:57.080 --> 00:02:58.330
That's why I'm here!

00:02:58.330 --> 00:03:00.950
Um... I have a question.

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:04.200
Could it be that you guys
aren't aiming to be number one?

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:06.580
You're okay not beating the team Shinozaki's on?

00:03:06.580 --> 00:03:07.580
What'd you say?!

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:10.240
Are you sayizng that if we
add him, then we can win?

00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:11.620
Who are you?

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:12.910
I haven't seen you around before.

00:03:12.910 --> 00:03:15.330
Hayato Sasugai, a first year.

00:03:15.330 --> 00:03:17.240
I want to join the club, too.

00:03:17.240 --> 00:03:20.790
Oh, not as a player, but as a coach.

00:03:20.790 --> 00:03:23.080
Do you know him?

00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:24.620
Maybe he's a transfer student.

00:03:24.620 --> 00:03:28.120
If you want to return to figure skating,
then you should be aiming for singles.

00:03:28.120 --> 00:03:29.990
I can introduce you to a club.

00:03:29.990 --> 00:03:31.580
There's no point in doing singles!

00:03:31.580 --> 00:03:33.910
I wanna beat Shinozaki!

00:03:35.830 --> 00:03:38.910
Coach, we'll be starting practice right away.

00:03:38.910 --> 00:03:39.740
Let's go!

00:03:39.740 --> 00:03:41.330
--Yes, sir!
--Okay.
--Huh? Right...

00:03:43.870 --> 00:03:44.870
Sho!

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:46.830
Do you feel the same way, Sho?

00:03:46.830 --> 00:03:50.200
Did you think you could be the ace
right away if you joined?

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:54.910
During the time you were away
from skating, we kept training.

00:03:54.910 --> 00:03:56.660
It's not the same as it was before.

00:04:01.990 --> 00:04:06.290
You don't have anything to say?
You're the coach, aren't you?

00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:10.200
Huh?!

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:12.200
Anyway, don't be so discouraged.

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:14.370
I'll think of a good way for us to joi--

00:04:14.370 --> 00:04:15.660
You've gotta be kidding me!

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:18.200
Like I can accept this!

00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:22.830
I need to teach him "stay" first, huh?

00:04:22.830 --> 00:04:24.990
I'm going running now!

00:04:32.660 --> 00:04:35.200
Modern training prioritizes
quality before quantity.

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:37.490
Rest is also a kind of training, you know.

00:04:37.490 --> 00:04:39.450
You were on the rink for
the first time in a while, right?

00:04:39.450 --> 00:04:41.080
I'm sure your muscles are sore.

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:43.990
I'm gonna start training for real soon.

00:04:43.990 --> 00:04:46.080
I can't stay still.

00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:48.990
Looks like your grandparents
are allowing you to skate again, huh?

00:04:48.990 --> 00:04:52.330
Yeah. Apparently, they were worried about me.

00:04:52.330 --> 00:04:54.040
Anyway, you should rest for today.

00:04:54.040 --> 00:04:55.660
Tomorrow, the real training will start.

00:04:55.660 --> 00:04:57.450
If you pass out, then--

00:04:57.450 --> 00:04:59.580
Hey, wait! Didn't I tell you to rest?

00:04:59.580 --> 00:05:02.080
Stay! Wait! Sit!

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:09.540
That guy...

00:05:16.950 --> 00:05:18.200
What the heck?

00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:20.540
Doesn't it seem like
he wants to join us after all?

00:05:25.040 --> 00:05:27.330
What do you think you're doing?

00:05:27.330 --> 00:05:29.040
Shut up. I'm practicing on my own.

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:30.660
You're in the way. Get out of here!

00:05:30.660 --> 00:05:32.740
Who cares? I told you, I'm practicing on my own.

00:05:42.370 --> 00:05:47.040
You know, there's a smarter way
to get them to let you join the club.

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:48.700
Shut up.

00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:52.830
I'm against it.

00:05:52.830 --> 00:05:54.790
There are only drawbacks to letting him join.

00:05:54.790 --> 00:05:58.330
But at this rate, the other members
won't be able to concentrate on practice.

00:05:58.330 --> 00:06:03.080
Maeshima's always been moody,
restless, and illogical.

00:06:03.080 --> 00:06:04.580
He'll get bored and quit in no time.

00:06:04.580 --> 00:06:07.950
Do you think a guy like you just
described could perform like he did?

00:06:12.990 --> 00:06:14.490
It's fine as long as he can become an asset.

00:06:14.490 --> 00:06:16.580
If he seems like he'll do harm,
then we make him quit.

00:06:16.580 --> 00:06:19.540
We just have to rein him in.

00:06:22.580 --> 00:06:24.240
You're the captain.

00:06:24.240 --> 00:06:25.990
You decide.

00:06:25.990 --> 00:06:27.700
Have you decided?

00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:28.740
Yeah...

00:06:30.450 --> 00:06:31.620
What'd you think?

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:34.330
It's like this jacket was made for me, right?

00:06:34.330 --> 00:06:36.240
You're still only a provisional member,
though, aren't you?

00:06:36.240 --> 00:06:39.620
If you'd left it to me,
we could've been official members.

00:06:39.620 --> 00:06:42.290
Don't worry about that!

00:06:42.290 --> 00:06:44.160
I don't have to practice
on the dirt in the park anymore.

00:06:44.160 --> 00:06:47.080
Starting today, I can practice on a real rink!

