00:06:50.540 --> 00:06:54.330
but everyone, do what it says on the paper
that's getting passed out to you right now.

00:06:58.200 --> 00:07:00.620
Do what you can without injuring yourself.

00:07:00.620 --> 00:07:03.120
Don't come asking me even
if you don't know something.

00:07:03.120 --> 00:07:05.490
I leave everything to your own initiative.

00:07:05.490 --> 00:07:06.330
That's it.

00:07:06.330 --> 00:07:09.580
Wait a minute! This is all just basic stuff!

00:07:09.580 --> 00:07:10.540
Are you dissatisfied?

00:07:10.540 --> 00:07:11.830
Of course I am!

00:07:11.830 --> 00:07:14.490
If you don't want to do it,
then feel free to quit.

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:20.290
Hey, keep your toes pointed at the same angle!

00:07:20.290 --> 00:07:22.080
Okay.

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:25.620
Damn it! Everything on
my sheet is for beginners!

00:07:25.620 --> 00:07:30.040
Captain: third year,
Shotaro Terauchi. Position: Guard.

00:07:30.040 --> 00:07:33.910
Vice-Captain: Itsuki Kiriyama,
also a third year. Lead.

00:07:33.910 --> 00:07:35.620
Akimitsu Mochizuki, second year.

00:07:35.620 --> 00:07:37.790
The only wing on the team.

00:07:37.790 --> 00:07:40.490
Sota Jonouchi. Second year, guard.

00:07:40.490 --> 00:07:43.410
Izumi Himekawa. First year, lead.

00:07:43.410 --> 00:07:44.620
The team's ace.

00:07:44.620 --> 00:07:47.740
Tomoyuki Kubota. First year, reserve.

00:07:47.740 --> 00:07:51.330
Sasugai, was it? Do you have a minute... Hm?

00:07:51.330 --> 00:07:54.620
The Ionodai team's data. It's correct, right?

00:07:54.620 --> 00:07:59.200
Third year, manager, and Akimitsu
Mochizuki's older brother--Yukimitsu.

00:07:59.200 --> 00:08:02.580
You retired due to an injury during
a growth spurt in middle school.

00:08:02.580 --> 00:08:03.910
It's too bad.

00:08:03.910 --> 00:08:08.290
If you had kept competing, you would've
been a guard to rival Captain Terauchi.

00:08:08.290 --> 00:08:11.240
You did a lot of research. Are you a stalker?

00:08:11.240 --> 00:08:14.700
He who controls information
controls everything, you know?

00:08:14.700 --> 00:08:16.990
What else do you have written there?

00:08:16.990 --> 00:08:22.390
Ionodai High School Skate-Leading Club

00:08:16.990 --> 00:08:22.740
Other than Jonouchi and Himekawa,
everyone was from the same club as Maeshima,

00:08:22.740 --> 00:08:27.040
and in last year's nationals,
they made it to the semifinals.

00:08:27.040 --> 00:08:28.660
And...

00:08:28.660 --> 00:08:31.910
Takumi Adachi, still actively
competing as a skater,

00:08:31.910 --> 00:08:36.160
coaching just for the year he's taking off
for rehab for his lower back.

00:08:36.160 --> 00:08:41.450
He's got all this raw talent in front of him.
He really won't teach them anything?

00:08:41.450 --> 00:08:45.330
Well, it's the perfect setting
for me to take over, though...

00:08:45.330 --> 00:08:45.670
Hey, wait--

00:08:45.670 --> 00:08:48.330
Okay, okay. That's enough playing coach for now.

00:08:48.330 --> 00:08:50.290
I'm not playing! I'm--

00:08:50.290 --> 00:08:52.910
We're really busy, you know.

00:08:50.290 --> 00:08:52.910
Huh? Wait, wait--

00:08:57.290 --> 00:08:59.160
Today's day ten, huh?

00:08:59.160 --> 00:09:02.450
I thought you'd snap and get mad right away,
but you've been pretty obedient.

00:09:02.450 --> 00:09:04.660
I'm a new club member, after all.

00:09:04.660 --> 00:09:06.580
I need to build stamina, too.

00:09:06.580 --> 00:09:08.160
How do you <i>really</i> feel?

00:09:08.160 --> 00:09:11.240
I didn't join the club to do this kind of stuff.

00:09:11.240 --> 00:09:13.370
I wanna jump more. I wanna skate more.

00:09:13.370 --> 00:09:15.620
Like at that exhibition...

00:09:15.620 --> 00:09:17.240
But, well...

00:09:17.240 --> 00:09:21.040
For a training plan designed by
that temporary coach, it makes sense.

00:09:21.040 --> 00:09:24.370
It's effective for someone like you
who's coming back after a long break.

00:09:24.370 --> 00:09:25.910
Try to keep going with it for now.

00:09:25.910 --> 00:09:28.160
Hey, Sasu!

00:09:28.160 --> 00:09:29.160
Coming!

00:09:29.160 --> 00:09:32.740
Jeez, I'm being treated like a manager.

00:09:34.080 --> 00:09:36.740
Thank you very much!

00:09:36.740 --> 00:09:38.160
See ya.

00:09:38.160 --> 00:09:40.620
Okay, Shima. Here's the key to this place.

00:09:40.620 --> 00:09:44.700
Up until now, it's been Tomo's job,
but starting today, it's your turn, Shima.

00:09:44.700 --> 00:09:46.830
The general public also uses this place,

00:09:46.830 --> 00:09:48.660
so make sure you take good care of it.

00:09:51.190 --> 00:09:55.150
The next day

00:09:52.790 --> 00:09:54.120
Maeshima?

00:09:54.120 --> 00:09:55.790
Where's Maeshima?

00:09:55.790 --> 00:09:59.290
Is he absent today? Has anyone heard from him?

00:09:59.290 --> 00:10:00.870
Maeshima's absent?

00:10:00.870 --> 00:10:05.160
Yes. It sounds like no one
contacted the school, either...

00:10:05.160 --> 00:10:07.160
Did he finally lose his nerve?

00:10:07.160 --> 00:10:09.120
No, I don't think so...

00:10:09.120 --> 00:10:10.240
Huh?

00:10:17.290 --> 00:10:18.580
That guy...

00:10:18.580 --> 00:10:20.620
Don't tell me he's been here since morning...?

00:10:20.620 --> 00:10:23.040
He's gotten better compared to before.

00:10:23.040 --> 00:10:26.160
But he hasn't had time to practice, has he?

00:10:46.580 --> 00:10:48.450
No way! A quintuple?

00:10:49.660 --> 00:10:53.870
Ow... The rink's all scratched up,
and the edge of my blade got caught...

00:10:56.370 --> 00:11:02.660
Oh, I'm sorry! I'll get
the Zamboni on the ice...

00:11:02.660 --> 00:11:04.990
You're expelled from the club.
Don't come back here again!

00:11:04.990 --> 00:11:06.080
Wh--?!

00:11:06.080 --> 00:11:08.080
Tomo, contact the custodian.

00:11:08.080 --> 00:11:09.080
Yes, sir!

00:11:09.080 --> 00:11:11.160
Why?! Why...?

00:11:11.160 --> 00:11:13.740
You didn't keep to the
training plan you were given,

00:11:13.740 --> 00:11:17.040
and with your selfish actions,
you wasted our practice time.

00:11:17.040 --> 00:11:19.830
As I thought, you are not
suited for team sports.

00:11:19.830 --> 00:11:21.580
We don't need you in our club.

00:11:21.580 --> 00:11:23.780
If you understand, then hurry up
and take your things and--

00:11:23.370 --> 00:11:24.830
What the hell?!

00:11:24.830 --> 00:11:27.950
Making me practice boring stuff day after day.

00:11:27.950 --> 00:11:30.450
I can do more! I can skate more!

00:11:30.450 --> 00:11:32.830
Look at what I can really do!

00:11:32.830 --> 00:11:34.790
You guys couldn't beat me before, right?

00:11:34.790 --> 00:11:37.990
So you should just shut up and follow me!

00:11:37.990 --> 00:11:39.120
Huh?

00:11:39.120 --> 00:11:40.370
Oh, man.

00:11:40.370 --> 00:11:43.540
Ken's talking about elementary school...

00:11:43.540 --> 00:11:46.330
It's that attitude of yours!

00:11:46.330 --> 00:11:49.080
Maeshima, get ready.

00:11:49.080 --> 00:11:52.990
If you can beat me, then I'll
let you join the club officially.

00:11:52.990 --> 00:11:57.240
I'll also propose that the coach
change your training plan.

00:11:57.240 --> 00:11:58.620
Terauchi!

00:11:58.620 --> 00:11:59.580
Seriously?

00:11:59.580 --> 00:12:02.950
But you understand what'll
happen if you lose, right?

00:12:02.950 --> 00:12:06.990
I've never lost to you
in a tournament before, Sho.

00:12:25.330 --> 00:12:26.330
Huh?

00:12:26.330 --> 00:12:28.790
Damn it, it's this late already?

00:12:28.790 --> 00:12:30.700
Practice has already started...

00:12:32.600 --> 00:12:35.200
Keyaki Park Ice Arena

00:12:49.040 --> 00:12:50.910
Hey, what happened?

00:12:50.910 --> 00:12:52.790
Oh, Sasugai!

00:13:02.540 --> 00:13:05.080
Oh? I see.

00:13:05.080 --> 00:13:06.490
It's strange, though.

00:13:06.490 --> 00:13:10.490
Ken performed really well at the exhibition,

00:13:10.490 --> 00:13:12.870
but in his match against the captain,
he kept messing up...

00:13:12.870 --> 00:13:14.410
How'd they compete?

00:13:14.410 --> 00:13:19.330
After being taught a routine, they had
ten minutes to practice before they started.

00:13:21.200 --> 00:13:22.950
Hey, Maeshima!

00:13:22.950 --> 00:13:25.620
First of all, don't underestimate
the basics, you idiot!

00:13:25.620 --> 00:13:28.540
And, you shouldn't be too confident in yourself.

00:13:28.540 --> 00:13:33.950
Well, we need that competitive spirit
of yours in our upcoming fight, though.

00:13:33.950 --> 00:13:35.290
I told you before--

00:13:35.290 --> 00:13:38.240
You have the ability to move
your body however you want

00:13:38.240 --> 00:13:41.040
and the ability to perfectly imitate
someone else's movements.

00:13:41.040 --> 00:13:45.660
But that's only if you can see it
and be inspired by watching it.

00:13:45.660 --> 00:13:49.370
You won't be able to visualize it well
if you're only taught it once.

00:13:49.370 --> 00:13:52.950
Well, it means your break from skating
is in the way of your visualization.

00:13:52.950 --> 00:13:55.290
It could also just be because
you're dumb. Dummy!

00:13:55.290 --> 00:13:56.240
Huh?!

00:13:56.240 --> 00:13:58.200
The training plan the coach made

00:13:58.200 --> 00:14:01.910
was to get your body to remember
how it moved before.

00:14:01.910 --> 00:14:04.620
I don't want to admit it,
but it's well thought out.

00:14:04.620 --> 00:14:06.240
Are you happy now?

00:14:06.240 --> 00:14:07.790
Hurry up and get off the rink.

00:14:07.790 --> 00:14:09.490
You're in the way of our practice.

00:14:11.540 --> 00:14:15.950
It was my fault this time for not taking
your personality into consideration.

00:14:15.950 --> 00:14:19.540
Sorry. I'll take responsibility.

00:14:19.540 --> 00:14:21.330
Hey, Kiriyama.

00:14:21.330 --> 00:14:23.870
If you're saying Maeshima
isn't suited to being on a team,

00:14:23.870 --> 00:14:26.660
then shouldn't you have a team match?

00:14:26.660 --> 00:14:27.910
And Captain Terauchi,

00:14:27.910 --> 00:14:31.120
you took advantage of the fact that your
opponent hadn't skated for a while to win.

00:14:31.120 --> 00:14:32.410
Are you really okay with that?

00:14:32.410 --> 00:14:34.120
What do you want to do?

00:14:34.120 --> 00:14:36.370
Let's have a match within the club.

00:14:36.370 --> 00:14:38.490
Your team versus ours.

00:14:38.490 --> 00:14:41.830
If we win, then you let us join officially.

00:14:41.830 --> 00:14:43.450
And if you lose?

00:14:43.450 --> 00:14:46.200
If that happens, then I'll drop out of Ionodai.

00:14:46.200 --> 00:14:47.080
Huh?

00:14:47.080 --> 00:14:48.330
You'll drop out of school?

00:14:48.330 --> 00:14:49.370
Are you serious?

00:14:49.370 --> 00:14:51.490
I think these are good stakes, though.

00:14:51.490 --> 00:14:54.040
Screw that! What're you thinking?

00:14:54.040 --> 00:14:55.490
Then I'll drop out, too!

00:14:55.490 --> 00:14:56.330
Huh?

00:14:56.330 --> 00:14:58.870
What are <i>you</i> thinking?
I'm going through all this--

00:14:58.870 --> 00:15:00.660
It's my problem to begin with!

00:15:00.660 --> 00:15:02.080
We made a pact, didn't we?

00:15:02.080 --> 00:15:04.540
We're in the same boat!

00:15:04.540 --> 00:15:07.120
Jeez. That's how it is,

00:15:07.120 --> 00:15:09.160
so please think about it carefully.

00:15:09.160 --> 00:15:12.790
Our futures are at stake here.

00:15:14.200 --> 00:15:17.240
Maeshima, you wanted to practice
something more interesting, right?

00:15:17.240 --> 00:15:21.160
You'd acknowledge that he's got
initiative then, right, Coach?

00:15:22.490 --> 00:15:28.540
Or will you cancel the match
and just allow us to join the club?

00:15:28.540 --> 00:15:30.740
We'll take that bet of yours.

00:15:30.740 --> 00:15:32.540
That's what you want, right?

00:15:32.540 --> 00:15:34.240
Great!

00:15:35.410 --> 00:15:38.080
The match will be a team match
with three on each team.

00:15:38.080 --> 00:15:39.990
It'll take place in a week.

00:15:39.990 --> 00:15:44.660
On your team will be Captain Terauchi,
Vice-Captain Kiriyama, and Akimitsu,

00:15:44.660 --> 00:15:46.950
with Yukimitsu on reserve.

00:15:46.950 --> 00:15:49.120
I'm retired, though?

00:15:49.120 --> 00:15:52.490
On our team, it'll be Maeshima,
Jonouchi, Himekawa,

00:15:52.490 --> 00:15:54.790
with Kubota on reserve.

00:15:54.790 --> 00:15:57.080
Three skaters who could be lead...

00:15:57.080 --> 00:15:59.740
It's not a very balanced choice.

00:15:59.740 --> 00:16:01.700
Are we giving him too much credit?

00:16:01.700 --> 00:16:04.870
I don't wanna be on the
same team as this guy, though.

00:16:04.870 --> 00:16:07.990
We don't really have time
to do this right now, do we?

00:16:07.990 --> 00:16:12.740
We'll decide positions and starting
team members based on this match.

00:16:12.740 --> 00:16:15.370
It's something we would've had to do anyway.

00:16:15.370 --> 00:16:17.200
That's all right with you, isn't it, Coach?

00:16:17.200 --> 00:16:18.290
Go ahead.

00:16:18.290 --> 00:16:21.200
That's how it is, Jonouchi, Himekawa.

00:16:21.200 --> 00:16:22.410
Got it, sir!

00:16:22.410 --> 00:16:23.240
Yes, sir.

00:16:23.240 --> 00:16:24.790
Then it's decided.

00:16:24.790 --> 00:16:29.540
That's how it is, so let's have
a planning meeting right away.

00:16:29.540 --> 00:16:30.700
Oh, right.

00:16:30.700 --> 00:16:34.910
Captain, during your slow jumps,
you should tighten your core more.

00:16:34.910 --> 00:16:37.620
Kiriyama, you should lift your head more.

00:16:37.620 --> 00:16:39.450
And Akimitsu, during your Choctaw,

00:16:39.450 --> 00:16:42.620
please put your right foot down
after you push your heel forward.

00:16:42.620 --> 00:16:43.910
What about me?

00:16:43.910 --> 00:16:45.450
I dunno.

00:16:45.450 --> 00:16:46.620
How mean...

00:16:46.620 --> 00:16:48.540
Are you trying to help the enemy?

00:16:48.540 --> 00:16:51.540
It's to make us more competitive in the future.

00:16:51.540 --> 00:16:53.120
I'm sorry, Coach.

00:16:53.120 --> 00:16:55.830
Yeah, this is a pain...

00:16:55.830 --> 00:17:01.450
But it won't look good if the team
falls apart the second I become coach.

00:17:01.450 --> 00:17:03.540
It can't be helped. Let's do it.

00:17:03.540 --> 00:17:05.450
Thank you, sir!

00:17:08.790 --> 00:17:10.080
I'm sorry!

00:17:10.080 --> 00:17:11.240
About what?

00:17:11.240 --> 00:17:15.120
Well, because of me...
you might have to drop out...

00:17:15.120 --> 00:17:18.580
You're the guy who added yourself
to it. What're you saying?

00:17:18.580 --> 00:17:21.160
But... can we really win?

00:17:21.160 --> 00:17:25.580
Everyone on the other team has regularly
made it to nationals since middle school.

00:17:25.580 --> 00:17:28.660
Their other guard went
to another school, though...

00:17:28.660 --> 00:17:31.700
I know. Taiga Himuro, right?

00:17:31.700 --> 00:17:34.950
He's the captain at Shinozaki's
high school right now.

00:17:34.950 --> 00:17:37.160
He's an elite skater at
a really prestigious school.

00:17:37.160 --> 00:17:38.990
Anyway, don't worry.

00:17:38.990 --> 00:17:41.660
I'm not in the habit of making bets I can't win.

00:17:41.660 --> 00:17:42.620
But...

00:17:42.620 --> 00:17:46.080
Oh, right, about our positions for the match...

00:17:51.950 --> 00:17:54.410
Wow, just doing what he said

00:17:54.410 --> 00:17:56.870
makes it a lot easier to skate
on the back outside edge.

00:17:56.870 --> 00:17:58.580
That Sasugai...

00:17:58.580 --> 00:18:02.490
He figured out our weaknesses
in such a short time?

00:18:02.490 --> 00:18:07.200
Oh, my, I guess that Sasu had reason to talk big.

00:18:07.200 --> 00:18:08.910
It can't be helped.

00:18:08.910 --> 00:18:11.660
I guess I have to do some
teaching of my own now.

00:18:13.700 --> 00:18:16.540
I'll be lead. I won't hear any objections.

00:18:16.540 --> 00:18:17.200
Huh?

00:18:17.200 --> 00:18:19.370
I started figure skating
to be popular with girls.

00:18:19.370 --> 00:18:20.910
In order to be popular, I need to stand out!

00:18:20.910 --> 00:18:23.290
In order to stand out, it's best
to be the star of skate-leading,

00:18:23.290 --> 00:18:25.370
the point-getter, the lead!

00:18:25.370 --> 00:18:28.200
But your position is guard...

00:18:28.200 --> 00:18:30.580
That's just temporary,
to hide from the public eye.

00:18:30.580 --> 00:18:32.700
It has nothing to do with you guys dropping out.

00:18:32.700 --> 00:18:35.290
I'm skating lead, no buts about it!

00:18:35.290 --> 00:18:38.410
What the hell? Then who'll be guard?

00:18:38.410 --> 00:18:39.740
Not my problem.

00:18:40.830 --> 00:18:41.300
You--

00:18:41.300 --> 00:18:42.290
I can't.

00:18:42.290 --> 00:18:46.240
I've never trained to do lifts,
and I don't plan to.

00:18:46.240 --> 00:18:50.080
Anyway, I have no intention of giving up
the lead to someone worse than me.

00:18:50.080 --> 00:18:52.870
Are you saying that I'm worse than you?

00:18:52.870 --> 00:18:54.660
Have you ever seen your own skating?

00:18:54.660 --> 00:18:56.330
Let's take this out front!

00:18:56.330 --> 00:18:58.160
No, thanks.

00:18:58.160 --> 00:19:01.870
Himekawa, you've been
like this ever since you joined!

00:19:01.870 --> 00:19:03.240
You should learn from Kubota...

00:19:03.240 --> 00:19:06.450
Why are you sitting there looking
like this has nothing to do with you?!

00:19:06.450 --> 00:19:08.660
This is your problem, too, you know.

00:19:08.660 --> 00:19:10.040
It's fine, it's fine.

00:19:10.040 --> 00:19:14.290
Why don't we see how practice goes
and decide positions after that?

00:19:14.290 --> 00:19:15.740
Yeah, I guess that makes sense.

00:19:15.740 --> 00:19:18.080
It won't do any good arguing about it here.

00:19:18.080 --> 00:19:19.870
What're acting all leader-like for,
you little first year?!

00:19:19.870 --> 00:19:20.590
He's right.

00:19:20.590 --> 00:19:21.330
Shut up!

00:19:21.330 --> 00:19:23.910
Ken, calm down! You'll cause
trouble for the restaurant!

00:19:23.910 --> 00:19:24.990
You should be quiet, too!

00:19:24.990 --> 00:19:26.240
No, <i>you</i> should be quiet, Maeshima!

00:19:26.240 --> 00:19:27.410
Huh?

00:19:29.160 --> 00:19:31.580
The coach really is amazing, huh?

00:19:31.580 --> 00:19:33.290
It's the first time he's taught us anything,

00:19:33.290 --> 00:19:36.120
but his directions were just right,
and there were a lot of variations.

00:19:36.120 --> 00:19:39.540
I feel like I dramatically improved
in just this one day.

00:19:39.540 --> 00:19:42.540
Don't get so excited that you hurt yourself.

00:19:42.540 --> 00:19:43.790
Hey.

00:19:43.790 --> 00:19:47.040
Are you worried about those guys?

00:19:47.040 --> 00:19:50.490
They're the ones who brought up
dropping out of school themselves.

00:19:50.490 --> 00:19:52.240
It's nothing for you to worry about.

00:19:52.240 --> 00:19:56.950
No, I was visualizing the
new performance in my head.

00:19:56.950 --> 00:19:58.040
I see...

00:19:59.580 --> 00:20:05.040
Like Himuro, Terauchi was also
scouted by St. Clavis Gakuin.

00:20:05.040 --> 00:20:09.790
But he gave that up to go to the same
high school as the rest of us.

00:20:09.790 --> 00:20:12.450
In order to aim for nationals with us...

00:20:12.450 --> 00:20:13.660
And now,

00:20:13.660 --> 00:20:17.790
a guy who took no notice of us
when we were novices

00:20:17.790 --> 00:20:22.040
comes shamelessly and
is messing everything up...

00:20:22.040 --> 00:20:24.330
I will <i>not</i> let him do that.

00:20:24.330 --> 00:20:26.120
There's no way I will.

00:20:26.120 --> 00:20:28.700
For Terauchi's sake, too, I'll--

00:20:28.700 --> 00:20:29.580
Hey--

00:20:29.580 --> 00:20:30.950
Your eyebrows are furrowing again.

00:20:30.950 --> 00:20:31.790
Stop that.

00:20:31.790 --> 00:20:33.990
What? We've known each other for a long time.

00:20:33.990 --> 00:20:34.990
Be quiet.

00:20:42.450 --> 00:20:44.580
What do you think of our school rink?

00:20:44.580 --> 00:20:45.870
I'm surprised.

00:20:45.870 --> 00:20:48.660
I never imagined a high school
would have their own rink like this.

00:20:48.660 --> 00:20:51.240
As expected of an invincible school.

00:20:51.240 --> 00:20:53.410
Kensei Maeshima.

00:20:53.410 --> 00:20:55.330
He quit figure skating for a while,

00:20:55.330 --> 00:20:57.740
but I heard he's returned to the sport recently.

00:20:57.740 --> 00:20:59.450
An acquaintance told me about it.

00:21:02.830 --> 00:21:03.870
And?

00:21:03.870 --> 00:21:05.330
At his high school,

00:21:05.330 --> 00:21:07.740
they're having a match
with their club members soon.

00:21:07.740 --> 00:21:09.330
Are you interested?

