00:21:16.540 --> 00:21:17.450
Wow.

00:21:17.450 --> 00:21:19.410
He really is good.

00:21:20.740 --> 00:21:23.950
In middle school, because his
team didn't score that high,

00:21:23.950 --> 00:21:25.990
no one really noticed him.

00:21:25.990 --> 00:21:29.410
But Himekawa's individual abilities
are pretty considerable.

00:21:29.410 --> 00:21:32.370
Maeshima, if you're aiming for number one,

00:21:32.370 --> 00:21:35.490
then he's one of the people
you'll have to beat, too.

00:21:37.330 --> 00:21:40.490
Even so, I'm not moving from the lead position.

00:21:40.490 --> 00:21:43.580
I'm also not planning on giving up my position.

00:21:43.580 --> 00:21:44.700
What did you say?

00:21:44.700 --> 00:21:46.790
Let me teach you about a thing called hierarchy.

00:21:46.790 --> 00:21:48.120
Wanna take it behind the school?

00:21:48.120 --> 00:21:50.490
No, thanks. Anyway,
we're not at school right now.

00:21:50.490 --> 00:21:51.370
You bastard!

00:21:51.370 --> 00:21:54.830
Stop! Please stop, Jonouchi, Himekawa!

00:21:54.830 --> 00:21:56.290
Aren't you getting fired up?

00:21:56.290 --> 00:21:58.990
You have to bring this team
together and win the match,

00:21:58.990 --> 00:22:02.830
and then beat the team Shinozaki is on,
or you won't be able to be number one.

00:22:02.830 --> 00:22:06.040
Yeah... I'm brimming with excitement...

00:23:36.010 --> 00:23:51.030
Next Time

00:23:36.010 --> 00:23:51.030
Self-Centered

00:23:36.040 --> 00:23:38.620
Your big brother...

00:23:38.620 --> 00:23:39.450
Yuki?

00:23:39.450 --> 00:23:41.870
Does he have any weaknesses
or anything wrong with him?

00:23:41.870 --> 00:23:43.040
Why are you asking?

00:23:43.040 --> 00:23:45.290
To like manipulate him, or take him in--

00:23:45.290 --> 00:23:47.370
Sasu, the laundry!

00:23:47.370 --> 00:23:49.200
Okay, okay, I'll take it in right now!

00:23:49.200 --> 00:23:50.990
<i>You're</i> the one being taken in.
